# pico_epaper

A Raspberry Pi Pico with a Waveshare Pico-ePaper-2.66 attached directly to its
headers. The board inherits the Pico ARM SDK platform and fixes a 152 by 296
native-orientation, black-and-white panel on SPI1.

Waveshare documents DIN on GP11, CLK on GP10, CS on GP9, DC on GP8, reset on
GP12, and busy on GP13. The display operates at 3.3 V and uses SPI mode 0.

https://www.waveshare.com/wiki/Pico-ePaper-2.66
